docs/WORKFLOW.md:1: ## Codex Execution Workflow
docs/WORKFLOW.md:2: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:3: - Codex work for the OAF Website must be launched from the OAF Website repository so the website and GraManna workstreams remain isolated.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4: - Codex prompts should normally be provided as a one-step PowerShell block that the owner can paste directly into the OAF Website terminal.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:5: - Use `Invoke-OAFCodex` for normal website Codex runs.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:6: - In the current PowerShell helper configuration, `Invoke-OAFCodex` copies Codex's final report to the clipboard automatically after a successful run.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:7: - `Invoke-OAFCodexClipboard` is not required merely to receive output on the clipboard; use it only when the prompt itself is being supplied through the clipboard.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:8: - Do not default to the VS Code F4 shortcut for website work unless the owner specifically requests it.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:9: - Every Codex prompt must clearly state that it is working only in the current OAF Website repository.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:10: - Codex must not commit or push changes unless an explicit approved commit checkpoint has been reached.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:11: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:12: ### Current Supported Codex Modes
docs/WORKFLOW.md:13: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:14: The current `Invoke-OAFCodex` helper accepts these modes:
docs/WORKFLOW.md:15: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:16: - `SOL / HIGH`
docs/WORKFLOW.md:17: - `SOL / EXTRA HIGH`
docs/WORKFLOW.md:18: - `SOL / MAX`
docs/WORKFLOW.md:19: - `ASTRA / EXTRA HIGH`
docs/WORKFLOW.md:20: - `ASTRA / MAX`
docs/WORKFLOW.md:21: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:22: Do not request unsupported modes such as `SOL / MEDIUM` unless the PowerShell helper is later updated to support them.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:23: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:24: ### Mandatory First-Failure Capture and Immediate Owner Reporting (Standing Rule)
docs/WORKFLOW.md:25: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:26: This **permanent workflow requirement** applies to future OAF Website Codex work,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:27: PowerShell/Python helpers, tests, migrations, integrations, scheduled jobs, and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:28: approved operational runs, including the OAF Website side of shared services.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:29: It supplements stricter feature-specific audit, privacy, authorization and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:30: recovery contracts. A generic `BLOCKED`, `FAILED`, exception or exit code is
docs/WORKFLOW.md:31: **not** a sufficient final diagnosis when a more specific result was observable.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:32: Implement diagnostic capture **before** asking the owner to execute a new or
docs/WORKFLOW.md:33: materially changed workflow; keep the implementation proportional to the task.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:34: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:35: - **Prepare evidence before risky operations.** Establish the approved
docs/WORKFLOW.md:36:   owner-controlled destination, a unique run/attempt identity, exclusively
docs/WORKFLOW.md:37:   created evidence files, and live terminal plus simultaneous complete
docs/WORKFLOW.md:38:   sanitized logging *before* the first step that could fail or cause side
docs/WORKFLOW.md:39:   effects. Initialize the established OAF visual alert/reporting capability
docs/WORKFLOW.md:40:   early enough to cover preflight failures. Never truncate, overwrite, or
docs/WORKFLOW.md:41:   silently merge historical runs. If evidence initialization fails, stop
docs/WORKFLOW.md:42:   safely and disclose the reporting limitation through any available channel.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:43: - **Record exactly where execution stopped.** Emit and flush a `STARTED` record
docs/WORKFLOW.md:44:   before each material gate or operation; finish it with `PASS`, `BLOCKED`
docs/WORKFLOW.md:45:   (evaluated and rejected), `ERROR` (could not evaluate), or `NOT_RUN` (not
docs/WORKFLOW.md:46:   reached because of a stated dependency). Include UTC timestamps, run and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:47:   package/artifact identity, stage, stable operation/predicate identifier and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:48:   relevant source/function. An unfinished `STARTED` record after interruption
docs/WORKFLOW.md:49:   means `INTERRUPTED/UNKNOWN`, **not** success or proof of no side effects.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:50: - **Retain actionable, sanitized details.** For every failed or blocked check,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:51:   record the expected condition and observed condition or `UNAVAILABLE`, the
docs/WORKFLOW.md:52:   exact constituent conflict code(s) rather than only an aggregate rejection,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:53:   and a safe exception class plus SQLSTATE, HRESULT or exit code when present.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:54:   Identify which prior checks passed, which dependent checks were not run, and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:55:   which operational boundaries were reached: task/process actions, database
docs/WORKFLOW.md:56:   mutation/commit certainty, provider submission/acceptance uncertainty, and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:57:   cleanup. Distinguish verified facts, hypotheses, and missing visibility.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:58: - **Persist before propagating failure.** Preserve reached-check results and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:59:   known side effects in bounded structured evidence, flush/synchronize using
docs/WORKFLOW.md:60:   the established durability mechanism, **then** raise or return the failure.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:61:   A nonzero Python/child exit must not hide already-published validated safe
docs/WORKFLOW.md:62:   diagnostics from its PowerShell/parent reporter. Validate evidence identity,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:63:   source, format and privacy before consuming it. Missing or malformed evidence
docs/WORKFLOW.md:64:   remains a failure with an explicit evidence gap, never implied success.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:65: - **Report immediately to the owner.** At the end of **every** Codex, test, or
docs/WORKFLOW.md:66:   authorized operational run, present a concise first-failure/blocked-step
docs/WORKFLOW.md:67:   summary directly in the visible terminal and Codex final report. Preserve
docs/WORKFLOW.md:68:   the complete sanitized simultaneous log and structured evidence location;
docs/WORKFLOW.md:69:   automatically copy the report to the clipboard with read-back verification
docs/WORKFLOW.md:70:   and display the existing OAF success/failure visual alert. Include run ID,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:71:   exact stopped stage/predicate, reason, safe expected/observed information,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:72:   completed/not-run steps, known or uncertain side effects, evidence path,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:73:   and the **single next safe checkpoint**. Do not announce success until the
docs/WORKFLOW.md:74:   required terminal evidence, log/transcript finalization and reporting checks
docs/WORKFLOW.md:75:   are complete. If clipboard, alert or logging fails, show a safe fallback and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:76:   explicitly label reporting **INCOMPLETE**; do not falsely claim delivery.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:77: - **Protect confidential data.** Never put passwords, tokens, API/DPAPI keys,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:78:   private capabilities/URLs, raw subscriber records, secret-bearing connection
docs/WORKFLOW.md:79:   strings, raw SQL parameters, unrestricted process arguments/environment
docs/WORKFLOW.md:80:   values, or unredacted exception text into terminal, clipboard, alerts, or
docs/WORKFLOW.md:81:   ordinary logs. Use fixed codes, bounded metadata, fingerprints and restricted
docs/WORKFLOW.md:82:   evidence locations where needed. Protect existing private evidence and ACLs.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:83: - **Fail closed; keep authority separate.** Recording a failure or finishing a
docs/WORKFLOW.md:84:   diagnostic collection does **not** authorize a retry, migration, worker,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:85:   provider send, task change, or reuse of consumed authority. Preserve claims,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:86:   outcomes, markers and uncertainty. Stop unsafe dependent operations, while
docs/WORKFLOW.md:87:   allowing only separately safe read-only checks approved by the current
docs/WORKFLOW.md:88:   contract. Do not fabricate missing observations or rewrite past failures.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:89: - **Validate the real reporting boundary before approval.** Test the actual
docs/WORKFLOW.md:90:   producer -> evidence writer -> child/parent consumer -> terminal/log/clipboard/
docs/WORKFLOW.md:91:   alert path, including early initialization failures, aggregate rejects,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:92:   nonzero child exits, partial logs, interrupted operations, publication errors
docs/WORKFLOW.md:93:   and finalization failure. Mocks may isolate genuine operational side effects,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:94:   but must not substitute away the reporting interface under test. An offline
docs/WORKFLOW.md:95:   PASS is not live readiness. Use focused, proportionate checks; avoid a new
docs/WORKFLOW.md:96:   framework, repeated broad test campaigns, or separate diagnosis for each
docs/WORKFLOW.md:97:   successive error.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:98: - **Codex instructions are mandatory.** Every future Codex prompt that builds,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:99:   changes or runs executable workflows must carry these requirements forward.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:100:   Review the captured diagnostic evidence immediately after a stop and supply
docs/WORKFLOW.md:101:   its actual first blocking reason in the final clipboard report; if the exact
docs/WORKFLOW.md:102:   cause is unknowable, identify the evidence gap and the smallest safe next
docs/WORKFLOW.md:103:   observation instead of declaring a root cause. Continue one approved prompt
docs/WORKFLOW.md:104:   and checkpoint at a time, without silently changing the established
docs/WORKFLOW.md:105:   PowerShell/Codex execution method.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:236: **Current scope supersedes historical Stage 1 status statements below.** The four policies A-D are owner-approved. Stage 4C development/testing migrators are CLOSED / DELIVERED / PASS as reported by the owner; this source task does not repeat live verification. Stage 5 operational adapter source and offline validation are authorized. Independent artifact approval is **pending**; owner-issued execution authorization is **pending**; live migration execution is **not authorized**. No real authorization record is issued by this task. No live credentials, PostgreSQL changes, package installation, staging, commits, or pushes are authorized.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:237: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:238: - **Policy A - destination and evidence:** Use `%LOCALAPPDATA%\OAF Website\BootstrapAudit\MigrationAudit\`, separate from Stage 4C records. The existing BootstrapAudit parent must be available; the adapter may create only its MigrationAudit child. Reject missing, relative, redirected, or unavailable destinations. JSON issuance, claim, denial, execution, and terminal records use exclusive creation, UTF-8/LF, flush, and file `fsync`, following the existing Windows implementation. Never overwrite history, including partial writes. Authorization issuance and terminal finalization also require completion evidence: exclusively write, flush, fsync, and close a pending completion record, then publish its completed name by an exclusive hard link. No synchronization follows that publication. If publication returns an error after creating the exact link, a read-only same-file check recognizes completed publication without retry. Retain both names; pending records are never accepted as completion. Unsupported publication fails closed. File synchronization does not promise protection against every filesystem, hardware, or power-loss failure. Record authorization, denial, execution phases, success, failure, and commit uncertainty. Allowlisted evidence excludes passwords, credential values, complete database URLs, private SQL parameters, raw exception text, and environment dumps.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:239: - **Policy B - retention:** Preserve approval, authorization, claim, and audit records until separate owner authorization permits archival or disposal. No automatic deletion, expiry cleanup, rotation, or claim removal. Expired authorizations remain evidence and cannot execute.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:240: - **Policy C - authorization:** Require a distinct, deliberate owner-issued record with a unique UUID, UTC issuance and expiry, and lifetime of at most 24 hours. Bind the exact environment, operation, expected starting state, target revision, independently approved manifest/revision hashes, applicable prerequisite approvals, and predecessor claim. Reject missing, malformed, future-dated, expired, reused, mismatched, or stale records. Revalidate the exact bound authorization UUID, bytes, and UTC validity at the final runner and Alembic pre-mutation boundaries and immediately before commit, after required audit persistence. Matching hashes prove integrity only. The runner consumes records and never issues or approves them. Issuance is separate from artifact approval, and neither authorizes another environment or a later no-op.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:241: - **Policy D - failure and recovery:** Required audit-write failure before mutation blocks execution. Authorization denial fails closed, with sanitized persistent evidence whenever the destination is available. An unavailable audit destination never permits continuation. Preserve an acknowledged commit as committed even if postcommit verification or audit fails; uncertainty stops without retry. Claims survive every failure and interruption. Complete, consistent evidence of verified success, verified no-op, or conclusive safe premutation failure permits a distinct newly authorized operation without exceptional reconciliation. Uncertain outcomes, postcommit audit failures, and incomplete or contradictory evidence require owner reconciliation before new authorization. Never delete claims, rotate credentials, stamp, repair, or blindly retry as automatic recovery.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:242: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:243: `FileOperationalAuthority` implements the existing `OperationalAuthority.authorize(request, run_id, artifacts) -> AuditSink` contract. The exact class is registered in `_OPERATIONAL_ADAPTER_TYPES`; protocol-shaped objects and subclasses cannot authorize work. The migration CLI accepts only an existing `--authorization-id`. Direct runner calls require the same concrete authority, and Alembic requires the runner's single-use context and the authority's actual request/run/sink binding. There is no fallback engine or direct Alembic execution permission. Repository-only `plan` performs integrity checks and grants no execution authority.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:244: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:245: The transition remains `base -> 0001_migration_baseline`, with the revision unchanged and metadata-only. A no-op must separately authorize `expected_start=0001_migration_baseline`; an authorization for `base` cannot silently adopt an already-applied state. Testing is the first future live target. Development requires its own authorization and a prerequisite approval citing a successful testing baseline validation run for the same artifact hashes. Existing environment/DB/role matching, exact WinVault targets, SCRAM expectations, owner assumption, schema-qualified metadata, transaction, lock, timeout, drift, and manifest checks remain required.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:246: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:247: ##### Local record format and future deliberate issuance
docs/WORKFLOW.md:248: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:249: These are source interface instructions for a later separately authorized owner action, not permission to create real approvals or execute now. All operational records stay outside Git in MigrationAudit. The issuer is `python -m oaf_website.migration_authority issue --specification <absolute-owner-specification-path> --owner-issue`; it never connects to PostgreSQL or reads credentials. It returns a UUID only after completed issuance is published; a readable authorization payload alone cannot be consumed. Publication is the completion point even if the process stops before delivering its response; never blindly reissue after an interrupted response. `python -m oaf_website.migrate` uses `--authorization-id <issued-uuid>` with its existing explicit request arguments. Do not run a live upgrade/downgrade during source validation.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:250: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:251: The minimal issuer reads a UTF-8 JSON specification with exactly four keys: `request`, `artifact_approval`, `prerequisite_approval`, and `expires_utc`. `request` has exactly `action` (`verify` or `upgrade`), `environment`, `expected_start`, `target`, `manifest_hash`, and `revision_hash`. Both approval references have exactly `id` (canonical UUID) and `sha256` (SHA-256 of the approval file's exact bytes). `expires_utc` must be UTC, later than issuance, and no more than 24 hours later. Manifest/framework/revision hashes retain the existing `sha256-utf8-lf` normalization; approval-file and predecessor-claim hashes use exact bytes.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:252: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:253: The issuer verifies separately supplied local approval records; it has no action for generating or approving them:
docs/WORKFLOW.md:254: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:255: - `artifact-approval-<uuid>.json`: exactly `format` (integer 1), `kind` (`artifact_approval`), `id`, `reviewer_id` (canonical UUID), `approved_utc` (UTC), `decision` (`approved`), `manifest_hash`, and `revision_hash`. Approval must precede authorization issuance and match the independently reviewed artifacts. The repository manifest remains `pending_independent_review`; a future independent approval is a separate evidence record, never a change inferred from digest matching.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:256: - `prerequisite-approval-<uuid>.json`: the same six common fields, with `kind=prerequisite_approval`, plus `environment`, `expected_start`, `approvals`, `predecessor`, `owner_reconciliation`, and `testing_validation_run`. `approvals` maps exactly `dependency_acceptance`, `bootstrap_validation`, `lock_and_timeouts`, `search_path_and_postconditions`, `recovery_procedure`, and `audit_policies` to UUID references to applicable reviewed approvals. These are explicit local attestations of those reviews, not automated proof of their substantive correctness. For testing, `testing_validation_run` is null; for development, it references a completed successful testing `upgrade` run with matching artifact hashes: either acknowledged commit with verified postconditions or a fully verified target no-op. Require published terminal completion bound to that run, authorization, claim, and exact acknowledged event bytes. A partial or success-looking terminal record never qualifies. After an exceptional testing outcome, the existing owner reconciliation prerequisite must bind the exact testing predecessor and verified DB state, followed by a fresh separately authorized testing operation and completed target validation. Reconciliation alone never rewrites a failed result or substitutes for testing validation or independent artifact approval.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:257: - `predecessor` has exactly `sequence` and `sha256`: initially integer 0 and null; thereafter the latest environment claim's integer sequence and exact-byte hash. Initially `owner_reconciliation=not_applicable`. After a claim, every new prerequisite approval binds that exact predecessor and expected DB state and is approved after the claim was written. Complete, consistent published evidence of verified success, verified no-op, or conclusive safe premutation failure permits `owner_reconciliation=not_applicable`; the proven continuation state must match the new expected start. Uncertain commits, postcommit audit failures, missing/incomplete evidence, contradictions, and unresolved drift require `owner_reconciliation=completed`. The owner must reconcile the outcome and verify database state under the approved lock/recovery procedure before making that exceptional attestation. Every successor still requires a distinct explicit single-use owner authorization; no existing record authorizes a retry or later no-op.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:258: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:259: The issuer exclusively writes `authorization-<uuid>.json` containing the bound request and approval references, UTC issuance/expiry, and predecessor. Execution exclusively writes `claim-<environment>-<eight-digit-sequence>.json` before credentials or engines. All contenders for the same environment/predecessor, including different authorization UUIDs, compete for the same deterministic file; only one can succeed. A stale authorization cannot advance to another slot. Partial claims remain evidence and can be reconciled by their exact-byte hash without being repaired or reused. Successful claim creation is followed by exclusively created numbered run events and `terminal-<run-uuid>.json`; denials use separate unique JSON records. Completion records use `pending-authorization-<uuid>.json` / `completed-authorization-<uuid>.json` and `pending-terminal-<run-uuid>.json` / `completed-terminal-<run-uuid>.json`. Their exact fields are `format=1`, `kind=record_completion`, `record` (payload filename), `sha256` (exact payload bytes), `authorization_id`, `run_id` (null for issuance), and `evidence` (empty for issuance; exact-byte claim and acknowledged event hashes for finalization). Only the completed name qualifies; publication never overwrites another record. No failed or uncertain operation is automatically retried.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:260: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:261: Local files controlled by the same Windows account are **not tamper-proof** against that account. UUID reviewer/authorization references, explicit issuance, and hashes do not provide signatures, cryptographic identity assurance, or proof that a different human performed review. Trusted Python code and the credential-holding account remain the security boundary; modifying private process state, deleting evidence, or using credentials for arbitrary SQL is outside the adapter's protection. Preserve independent review and owner control as administrative prerequisites.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:262: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:263: ##### Stage 5 offline validation and deterministic autonomy
docs/WORKFLOW.md:264: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:265: Run the dedicated website `.venv` interpreter with `PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1`, empty `PYTEST_ADDOPTS`/`PYTEST_PLUGINS`, repository plus tests on `PYTHONPATH`, and `-B -m pytest -p migration_offline -q`. Explicitly select all eight test files: `tests/test_database_config.py`, `tests/test_migration_config.py`, `tests/test_migration_artifacts.py`, `tests/test_migration_authorization.py`, `tests/test_migration_catalog.py`, `tests/test_migration_runner.py`, `tests/test_migration_provenance.py`, and `tests/test_migration_operational.py`. The plugin blocks credential/network/database access before collection, guards real BootstrapAudit file reads, and redirects operational file tests to temporary directories. Approval and authorization records in tests are synthetic. No live Alembic operation or real owner issuance is part of these checks.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:266: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:267: Deterministic autonomy review: environment/request selection, approval/hash binding, UTC expiry, claim competition, denial persistence, audit transitions, transaction/commit classification, no-op checks, and recovery blocking use fixed rules without AI. Independent review, deliberate owner issuance, prerequisite attestation, and exceptional reconciliation remain the approved administrative boundaries. Offline success proves tested source behavior only; live PostgreSQL semantics, operational validation, independent artifact approval, and a later testing-only execution authorization remain separate gates.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:268: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:269: ##### Historical Stage 1 contract context
docs/WORKFLOW.md:270: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:271: The following Stage 1 approval/status and unresolved-policy wording is preserved as checkpoint history. For migration policies, source implementation, Stage 4C delivery, and the current authorization boundary, the Stage 5 entry above is controlling; it does not reopen policies A-D or grant live execution.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:272: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:273: **APPROVED DESIGN / NOT IMPLEMENTED:** The owner approved the Checkpoint 4 Candidate C migration-authority contract with three refinements: one approved revision per execution in one transaction; migration credential services ending in `/Migrations`; and deterministic, sanitized audit evidence. The specific architecture and staged sequence are governed by the "PostgreSQL Migration Authority Contract ∩┐╜?" Checkpoint 4" section in `WEBSITE_PLAN.md`.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:274: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:275: #### Authorization and Preservation
docs/WORKFLOW.md:276: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:277: - Stage 1 authorizes contract documentation only, limited to `docs/WORKFLOW.md` and `docs/WEBSITE_PLAN.md`. It authorizes no backend implementation, database provisioning/bootstrap, credential changes, package installation, staging, commit, or push.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:278: - Every future implementation stage requires separate explicit owner authorization. Completing a stage does not authorize the next stage. Design approval does not authorize execution or establish operational readiness.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:279: - No Request Your State feature tables or endpoints, email notification implementation, or production provisioning are authorized by this migration contract.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:280: - Before editing, read both governing documents completely, confirm the repository and branch, record HEAD, inventory staged/unstaged/untracked changes, and inspect existing target-document changes.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:281: - Preserve all pre-existing owner-authored modifications without renewed confirmation. They must accompany approved work at the next authorized commit checkpoint unless the owner explicitly excludes them. Do not discard, revert, overwrite, or stage them during documentation work.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:282: - Stage 1 validation is bounded: confirm only the authorized documents were changed by the task and previous changes remain intact; inspect the documentation diff; check consistency of role, credential, transaction, authorization, and status language; check for sensitive values; and run `git --no-pager diff --check`. Do not run broad tests for this stage.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:283: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4388: ## WU2 - OAF typed web launch implementation (2026-10-26)
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4389: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4390: Implementation and focused offline validation PASS. Activation stays OFF. Reuse
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4391: accepted WU1 integration/CI evidence; no cross-repository inspection or WU1
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4392: implementation reopening occurs in this unit.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4393: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4394: The existing authenticated release-event intake additionally accepts exactly
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4395: platform `web`, release_id `gramanna-web`, content_version `web-launch-v1` in the
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4396: same nine-field original payload. Stable UUID normalization, environment-bound
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4397: release credentials, immutable event/digest/cutoff, replay and append-only
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4398: correction/withdrawal authority remain unchanged. No recipients or message copy
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4399: can be supplied by the caller.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4400: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4401: An owner-approved canonical public HTTPS URL is required, with exact equality at
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4402: HTTP validation, persistence and rendering. Supply that same approved value to
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4403: `create_app(..., web_launch_url=...)` and to the existing processor's environment
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4404: as `GRAMANNA_WEB_LAUNCH_URL`, separately for the matching environment. There is no
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4405: default production URL. Missing configuration rejects web events and prevents web
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4406: rendering. Syntax rejects local/IP addresses, userinfo, ports, queries, fragments
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4407: and the accepted Android/iOS store destinations. No URL resolution or fetch occurs.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4408: The existing prohibition on extra `OAF_` database environment settings is retained.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4409: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4410: The existing `web_launch` preference, active consenting lifecycle, verification
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4411: and preference-grant timestamps, suppression and final locked eligibility recheck
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4412: select the audience no later than the original cutoff. Late signups, verification
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4413: and grants are excluded. Pending/claimed work honors withdrawal; attempted and
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4414: uncertain outcomes and original cutoff survive corrections, retry and recovery.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4415: The fixed text/HTML web-launch-v1 subject is `GraManna is now available on the web`;
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4416: it uses the configured URL and existing OAF sender and management/unsubscribe
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4417: footer. There is no caller-selected template, recipient list or Send action.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4418: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4419: The existing processor/scheduler/ReleaseDispatcher/Brevo path discovers up to three
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4420: independent launches. One invocation permits 10 confirmation submissions and at
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4421: most three submissions each for Android, iOS and web (19 total). No second worker,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4422: queue, role grant, delivery/subscriber/approval table or scheduler change is added.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4423: The additive `0008_web_launch`, directly after `0007_release_approvals`, replaces
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4424: only the existing platform/content checks and types web identity/content together.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4425: Exact artifact, catalog, dependency and audit revision validation includes it;
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4426: 0001 through 0007 files and historical revision entries remain byte-for-byte
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4427: preserved. Approval status remains pending_independent_review. No migration or
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4428: real authorization/approval issuance occurs; synthetic fixture authority stays in
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4429: isolated temporary test directories.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4430: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4431: Focused guarded validation: 922 primary cases plus three targeted coverage cases
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4432: PASS; an earlier three-case correction recheck also PASS. Zero unexpected external
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4433: access in every test attempt. Coverage of new/materially changed statements
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4434: (including enclosing multiline calls) and successor revision is 126/126 statements
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4435: and 112/112 branches, 100%, with no exclusions. Unchanged behavior reuses accepted
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4436: WU1 evidence. No full canonical, browser, live PostgreSQL or provider campaign was
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4437: run. Offline catalog fixtures do not certify live PostgreSQL rendering/readiness.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4438: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4439: Evidence: `.pytest_cache/wu2-web-20261027T044519Z-2080d85d/`. The first failure at
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4440: 2026-10-27T04:54:46.446586Z was a negative-case fixture passing `platform` twice;
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4441: 125 cases had passed, dependent coverage/final acceptance were NOT_RUN at that
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4442: stop. Corrected related fixture, environment-setting compatibility and temporary
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4443: harness issues retain their original logs and failure reconciliation. A short
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4444: unique test temporary directory avoids Windows audit-file path limits. Final
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4445: required focused validation and coverage gates all pass.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4446: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4447: The proportional security/deterministic-autonomy review PASS: fixed server rules,
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4448: authenticated environment-bound authority, no destination fetch, existing consent
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4449: and uncertainty controls, durable audit and bounded existing processing. No AI
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4450: runtime dependency is introduced. Owner-approved URL configuration, independent
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4451: exact-artifact review, separately authorized migration and later activation remain
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4452: operational dependencies, with no credentials/database/provider/email/service/task
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4453: changes, GraManna edits, deployment or Git delivery performed here.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4454: `Invoke-OAFCodex` is unchanged and alone owns final clipboard/read-back/alert;
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4455: there are no interim clipboard writes or visual alerts.
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4456: 
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4457: ONE next GraManna implementation action: connect its existing official web-launch
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4458: approval/correction/withdrawal lifecycle to this typed OAF event contract, retaining
docs/WORKFLOW.md:4459: original stable IDs/cutoff and automatically retrying only unconfirmed handoffs.
